\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces IMS aggregate$-$decimate lead-time difference under the original (2004-04-08) and corrected (2004-04-18) third-test failure labels, all ten detectors. Run differences are (\texttt  {1st\_test}, \texttt  {2nd\_test}, \texttt  {3rd\_test}) in hours, collapsing the five within-run sampling factors to one mean difference per run (Section~\ref  {sec:statproto}). $n_+/n_-/0$ counts positive, negative and exactly-zero runs; zero-difference runs are excluded from the sign test, so $n_{\text  {eff}}$ is the effective sample size under the original label. ``Floor'' is the smallest two-sided exact sign-test $p$ attainable at that $n_{\text  {eff}}$. Both arms use the 49-dimensional invariant feature schema, so the contrast isolates the label.\relax }}{26}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:d17label}{{14}{26}}
